<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner pulp unit wins worldwide deals.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner pulp unit wins worldwide deals.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Monday its pulp and paper division had been awarded contracts totalling 1.7 billion crowns ($237.7 million) in the last few weeks.</p>
<p>In a statement to the Oslo bourse, Kvaerner said the contracts were awarded in the United States, southeast Asia and Europe.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41 ($ = 7.153 Norwegian Crowns)</p>
</text>
